---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Ribose Contribution Management">
  <section class="py-8">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Ribose Contribution Management</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-sans text-3xl font-bold leading-snug md:text-4xl">
      Contributor License Agreements for the GitHub organizations of Ribose Inc.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed">
      Ribose publishes software whose licenses record the terms under which
      contributions are accepted. The Ribose Contribution Management service
      records those terms as Contributor License Agreements, applies the
      agreements to each pull request across the GitHub organizations of
      Ribose Inc., and reports the result of the evaluation as a status
      check on the pull request.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed">
      A pull request whose contributors have no agreement on record cannot be
      merged, because the license grants that the projects rely on would be
      incomplete. The service comments on such a pull request with the steps
      that each contributor can take, and it re-evaluates the pull request
      after a signature or an approval is recorded.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
    <h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold">The agreements</h2>
    <dl class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <dt class="font-semibold">
          The Individual Contributor License Agreement (ICLA)
        </dt>
        <dd class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          The ICLA is executed by a person who contributes in a personal
          capacity, and it covers the present and future contributions of
          that person. The person elects at signing whether the agreement
          also covers their previous contributions.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="font-semibold">
          The Organization CLA (OCLA)
        </dt>
        <dd class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          The OCLA is executed by an organization whose employees contribute
          on its behalf. The organization designates the employees who are
          authorized to contribute through its Schedule A, and the Point of
          Contact of the organization manages that list through the service.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="font-semibold">
          Staff and contractors
        </dt>
        <dd class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Employees of Ribose are covered by their employment, and their
          employment status is resolved through the identity service at
          id.ribose.com. Contractors are not covered by employment; a contractor
          executes an ICLA, or joins the Organization CLA of the organization
          that engages them.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
    <h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold">Signing</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <a
        href="/icla"
        class="rounded-sm border border-line bg-paper dark:bg-ink-2 p-6 transition-colors hover:border-brand-400"
      >
        <h3 class="font-semibold">Sign the ICLA</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          The service binds the signature to a Ribose ID account and to a
          verified GitHub handle, and it records the exact edition of the
          agreement together with the SHA-256 hash of the text.
        </p>
        <span class="mt-3 inline-block text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400">Open the signing page</span>
      </a>
      <a
        href="/organizations"
        class="rounded-sm border border-line bg-paper dark:bg-ink-2 p-6 transition-colors hover:border-brand-400"
      >
        <h3 class="font-semibold">Join an Organization CLA</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          An employee whose organization has executed an OCLA requests
          coverage for their GitHub handle; the Point of Contact of the
          organization approves the request before coverage begins.
        </p>
        <span class="mt-3 inline-block text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400">Request coverage</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-8">
    <h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold">Contributing through a pull request</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed">
      A contributor who prefers to begin from the pull request writes the
      comment
      <code class="rounded-sm bg-ink-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-ink dark:text-white">@ribose-cla agree</code>
      on the pull request. The service replies with a link that completes the
      signature, and the status check of the pull request is updated after
      the signature is recorded. A pull request whose contributors are
      covered by multiple agreements carries an additional step, in which
      the contributor states under which agreement the contribution is made;
      the service records that statement and cites it in the comment that it
      posts after the pull request is merged.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
